@startuml
title Smart Risk Assessment and Safety Resource Recommendation Module

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Times New Roman
skinparam defaultFontSize 15
skinparam ArrowColor #3F3F46
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EAF3FA
  BorderColor #6B8EAD
  FontColor #20242A
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #20BFA9
  StartColor #000000
  EndColor #000000
  BarColor #D6B81F
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFF8D9
  BorderColor #D8B84B
  FontColor #40351A
}

|#F7E8F5|Event Organiser|
start
:Submit or resubmit\nevent application;

|#E7F1FB|Smart Risk Assessment and Safety Resource Recommendation Module|
:Receive submitted event application;
:Retrieve submitted event data;
:Check required fields, evidence references\nand assessment eligibility;
if (Assessment input\nready and eligible?) then (No)
  :Record incomplete, blocked, or\nreview-required status;
  stop
else (Yes)
  :Prepare assessment request using the\nactive rubric, hard rules, and guidance;
endif

fork
  |#E5F7E6|Firestore Database|
  :Provide venue capacity and\nrelevant safety context;
  :Provide eligible historical-event\nand verified incident records;
fork again
  |#FFF9C9|External Services|
  :OpenWeather API provides\nevent-date weather data;
  :Public Holiday Dataset provides\nlocal date and holiday context;
end fork

|#E7F1FB|Smart Risk Assessment and Safety Resource Recommendation Module|
:Assemble contextual evidence snapshot\nwith source, time, eligibility, and provenance;

|#FFF9C9|External Services|
:Receive allowlisted event data, context,\nrubric, hard rules, and guidance;
:MiniMax M3 identifies hazards and proposes\ncategory likelihood and severity scores;

|#E7F1FB|Smart Risk Assessment and Safety Resource Recommendation Module|
:Validate AI response schema, categories,\nscores, evidence references, and rubric;
if (AI response valid and usable?) then (Yes)
  :Apply hard-rule constraints and\ncalculate official category risk values;
  :Calculate official overall score\nand Low, Medium, or High risk level;
  :Record AI proposal, adjustments,\nwarnings, rationale, and confidence;
  :Generate baseline safety-resource\nquantities and planning ranges;
else (No / unavailable)
  :Record validation warnings and mark\nAI analysis unavailable or retryable;
  :Do not fabricate category scores;\nroute the assessment to authorised manual review;
endif

note right
  MiniMax is advisory. It cannot replace the
  official result, hard rules, or authority decision.
end note

:Consolidate assessment readiness,\ncompliance, evidence confidence, AI status,\nand resource recommendations;

|#E5F7E6|Firestore Database|
:Verify the submitted input and\nprocessing claim are still current;
if (Input and claim still current?) then (No)
  :Discard stale result and retain\nwarning/audit provenance;
  stop
else (Yes)
  :Store assessment, evidence snapshot,\nAI analysis, resource recommendation,\nand version/provenance records;
  :Write audit entries and update\ncurrent assessment/resource references;
endif

|#E7F1FB|Smart Risk Assessment and Safety Resource Recommendation Module|
:Publish role-appropriate assessment outputs;

fork
  |#F7E8F5|Event Organiser|
  :View Assessment Summary;
fork again
  |#F2E7FA|Authority Officer|
  :View Risk Assessment and\nSafety Resource Recommendation;
  :Continue human approval review in\nthe Authority Approval and Notification Module;
  note left
    The module output supports review only.
    It does not create the authority decision.
  end note
end fork

stop
@enduml
